# ============================================================================
# Data — large reference files, GWAS sumstats, etc. (140GB+)
# ============================================================================
# Large external inputs stay out (GWAS sumstats, MAGMA binaries, NWB recordings).
# The small files Figure 4's exporters need ARE tracked, so the panel CSVs can be
# rebuilt from a clone -- see genetics/data/README.md.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/seaad_supertype_colors.json
!data/patchseq/
data/patchseq/*
!data/patchseq/README.md
!data/patchseq/swc/
data/patchseq/swc/*
!data/patchseq/swc/1079568285_upright.swc
!data/patchseq/swc/819770858_upright.swc
!data/patchseq/swc/1037461069_upright.swc
!data/patchseq/swc/758996755_upright.swc
!data/patchseq/swc/797048104_upright.swc

# The MAGMA chain is code, not data: these two build the gene-level analysis
# behind Fig. 4a/b, S9 and S10 from the Bigdeli GWAS-VCF. The sumstats they read
# (BCF 533 MB, .pval 316 MB) stay untracked.
!data/gwas/
data/gwas/*
!data/gwas/make_magma_input.sh
!data/gwas/magma_bigdeli/
data/gwas/magma_bigdeli/*
!data/gwas/magma_bigdeli/run_magma_bigdeli.sh

# ============================================================================
# Intermediate results — large matrices, npz files (1.3GB)
# Exception: the small Sst mean-expression slice + its provenance note are
# tracked, so Figure 4 is reproducible without the external enrichment repo.
# (Pattern must be `dir/*`, not `dir/`, or git will not descend to see the
#  negations below.)
# ============================================================================
results/intermediates/*
!results/intermediates/README.md
# Figure 4 (A9 rebuild): the enrichment result, the taxonomy match and the
# type-name map are small and are what r_panels/MANIFEST.tsv checksums, so
# they are tracked. The matrices they derive from (specificity 160 MB,
# Siletti cluster matrix 215 MB, pooled A9 means 81 MB) stay untracked and
# are regenerated by scripts/figures/{siletti_l2_log1p,build_spec_a9rbh}.py
# Figure 4 robustness supplement: the two alternative enrichment runs and
# the MTG type-name map. The specificity matrices behind them (158 MB each)
# stay untracked and are rebuilt by build_spec_mtg_sametax.py.
# SEA-AD-only taxonomy (2026-08-31, L. Duncan's ask): the gsa outputs + namemaps
# that export_panels_abc.py, export_fig4_robustness.py and
# export_supp_enrichment_seaad125.py read. The spec matrices (37-74 MB) and the
# per-supertype mean tables (68-74 MB) stay out; build_spec_seaad_only.py remakes them.
# MTG-era per-supertype means: no longer read by Figure 4, but still the input
# to the reserve MTG-vs-DLPFC baseline check (reserve/sst_strata_supp/).
!results/intermediates/seaad_sst_supertype_mean_expression.csv
!results/intermediates/T_a9only_bigdeli.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/T_a9only_pgc3.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/T_mtgonly_bigdeli.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/T_mtgonly_pgc3.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/namemap_a9only.csv
!results/intermediates/namemap_mtgonly.csv
!results/intermediates/a9_sst_supertype_mean_expression_cp10k.csv

